   "text": {
    "L1": "An angle is the amount of turn between two rays that start at the same point.",
    "L2": "That common point is the vertex, and the two rays are the arms.",
    "L3": "The size of an angle depends on the turn, not on the length of its arms.",
    "L4": "Here is a common mistake: longer arms make a bigger angle. That is not true because extending an arm does not change its direction or the turn.",
    "L5": "To compare angles, put their vertices together and place one arm on top of the other.",
    "L6": "Then compare where the second arms point. The one turned further out makes the bigger angle.",
    "L7": "In the worked example, both angles share the 12 hand; compare how many hour-spaces the other hand has turned."
   },
